        "zh-Hant": "未知圖騰"
      },
      "description": {
        "fun": "Unown are flat, black, one-eyed Pokémon shaped like letters: 26 forms for the Latin alphabet, plus an exclamation mark and a question mark added in Generation 3. They cling to the walls of ruins like ancient inscriptions, and alone they're weak, but gathered in numbers they're said to release an odd power. Ken Sugimori designed them because he wanted a more surreal Pokémon.",
        "guide": "A Psychic-type Pokémon shaped like a letter with a single eye, found mostly in ruins such as Johto's Ruins of Alph. It has 28 forms, one for each letter of the Latin alphabet plus ! and ?. It does not evolve.",
        "tagline": "A living alphabet that lines the walls of ancient ruins",
        "sources": [
          {
            "title": "Bulbapedia: Unown (Pokémon)",
            "url": "https://bulbapedia.bulbagarden.net/wiki/Unown_(Pok%C3%A9mon)"
          }
        ]
      },
